# Every plugin and application in this collection is its OWN repository, cloned
# as a sibling of this file. What this repository tracks is what belongs to the
# collection rather than to any one plugin: the conventions, the documentation
# style, the workspace configuration, and the site under `docs/`.
#
# Listed one by one rather than as `omdsh-*/`, for the same reason
# `pnpm-workspace.yaml` lists its members one by one: a glob decides the
# question for directories that do not exist yet, and a future directory that
# belongs to the collection would be ignored silently.
#
# Without these entries git records each checkout as a gitlink — a commit
# pointer to a repository nobody can resolve from this one — which looks like a
# tracked directory until somebody clones and finds it empty.
omdsh-base/
omdsh-chatmode/
omdsh-codemode/
omdsh-desktop/
omdsh-editor/
omdsh-eyes/
omdsh-office/
omdsh-plughub/
omdsh-remctrl/
omdsh-remdev/
omdsh-shortcuts/
omdsh-sidechat/
omdsh-sidepanel/
omdsh-status/
omdsh-tui/
omdsh-usage/
omdsh-webapp/

# The catalog is its own repository too, and the hub reads it over the network
# rather than from here. `registry/build.mjs` still runs from this checkout,
# because it reads the siblings above.
registry/

# So is the profile repository — `omdsh-plugins/.github`, whose `profile/README.md`
# is what https://github.com/omdsh-plugins shows above the repository list.
# `scripts/build-profile.mjs` writes into a checkout of it here, under a name of
# its own: a directory called `.github` is this repository's workflows.
org-profile/

# pnpm installs the whole workspace closure here.
node_modules/

.DS_Store

# pnpm drops its content-addressable store here when no global store is configured.
.pnpm-store/
